WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.294
Governments, regulators, customers,

00:00:01.294 --> 00:00:04.874
and industry groups increasingly emphasize software supply chain transparency.

00:00:04.874 --> 00:00:10.842
SBOMs are one way organizations can demonstrate that they understand the components inside their software.

00:00:10.842 --> 00:00:15.218
SBOM expectations may appear in procurement, vendor risk management, customer assurance,

00:00:15.218 --> 00:00:17.605
secure development programs, or regulatory conversations.

00:00:17.605 --> 00:00:21.185
The exact requirements vary by organization, sector, and contract.

00:00:21.185 --> 00:00:25.562
For procurement teams, an SBOM can support questions about third-party software.

00:00:25.562 --> 00:00:27.153
What components are included?

00:00:27.153 --> 00:00:28.744
Are there unsupported dependencies?

00:00:28.744 --> 00:00:32.325
How does the vendor manage vulnerabilities in supplied components?

00:00:32.325 --> 00:00:34.314
For compliance and governance teams,

00:00:34.314 --> 00:00:39.088
SBOMs can provide evidence of software inventory practices and supply chain visibility.

00:00:39.088 --> 00:00:43.066
They can support broader programs that manage security, privacy, operational,

00:00:43.066 --> 00:00:44.260
or contractual risk.

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:46.647
For customers, SBOMs can improve transparency.

00:00:46.647 --> 00:00:49.830
A customer may not need every internal detail,

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:55.002
but structured component information can help them evaluate risk and ask better questions.

00:00:55.002 --> 00:00:57.389
SBOMs do not make trust automatic.

00:00:57.389 --> 00:01:00.969
Trust still depends on secure development practices, vulnerability management,

00:01:00.969 --> 00:01:04.948
incident response, vendor governance, documentation, and honest communication about risk.

00:01:04.948 --> 00:01:10.119
Organizations should treat SBOM compliance drivers as part of a larger operating model.

00:01:10.119 --> 00:01:13.302
The goal is not simply producing a file,

00:01:13.302 --> 00:01:16.485
but maintaining reliable software transparency that supports decisions.

00:01:16.485 --> 00:01:20.065
This is especially important when customers ask for SBOMs.

00:01:20.065 --> 00:01:25.237
A mature response includes clear scope, current data, a way to explain limitations,

00:01:25.237 --> 00:01:28.420
and a process for handling follow-up questions responsibly.
